Revision history for Perldantic

0.01  2026-09-24
    - First release: pydantic's data validation for Perl, on a Python-free Rust port of
      pydantic-core (base commit 0384c970e, see NOTICE and upstream/UPSTREAM.md in the
      repository).
    - Models declared the Moo way (`use Perldantic`, has, extends, with, roles, BUILD,
      method modifiers) with pydantic's model_validate, model_validate_json, model_dump,
      model_dump_json, model_json_schema, model_copy, model_fields_set and model_extra.
    - Types with Types::Standard names: Any, Undef, Bool, Int, Num, Str, Bytes, Decimal,
      Date, Time, DateTime, Duration, Uuid, Url, MultiHostUrl, Maybe, Optional, ArrayRef,
      Set, Json, Chain, Tuple, HashRef, Map, Dict, Enum, Literal, InstanceOf, unions with `|`
      and AnyOf, discriminated unions; pydantic's constraints through `has` options or
      `->with`; Type::Tiny constraints wherever a type is expected.
    - field_validator, model_validator, field_serializer, model_serializer and
      computed_field, with pydantic's modes and info objects.
    - Perldantic::TypeAdapter for any type: validate, validate_json, dump, dump_json,
      json_schema.
    - Structured exceptions (Perldantic::ValidationError and friends); errors for Perl data
      use Perl's vocabulary (hash_type, array_type, undef_required, ...).
    - Value classes Perldantic::Date, ::Time, ::DateTime, ::Duration, ::Uuid, ::Url and
      ::MultiHostUrl; Math::BigFloat for decimals; DateTime and Time::Moment interop.
    - Perldantic::FFI: the core schema API itself (validators and serializers for
      pydantic core_schema dicts, JSON Schema).
    - check / model_check: validation without building a result.
    - Lazy objects, opt-in (`lazy => 1` per call, `model_config lazy => 1`, or a
      TypeAdapter's config): validated data stays in the core until an object is read,
      about 10x faster than building Moo objects.
    - Performance: validation reads Perl data in place and builds objects in C (5x faster
      than Moo + Type::Tiny::XS on docs/BENCHMARKS.md's models; check 2.5x faster than
      Type::Tiny::XS's check).
    - Documentation: POD for every module, docs/MIGRATING_FROM_PYDANTIC.md,
      docs/DIVERGENCES.md.
